/**
 * Pendle R5d PRICE-FLOOR fixtures — RAW `POST /v3/sdk/{chainId}/convert` response
 * bodies for the SIX new write actions, captured verbatim from the LIVE hosted
 * API. Nothing here is synthesized.
 *
 * These are the R5d siblings of `./floor-fixtures.ts`, kept in their own module
 * so the R5a captures that pin the nine shipped selectors stay byte-unchanged.
 *
 * PROVENANCE
 *   Command  : POST {base}/v3/sdk/{chainId}/convert, body
 *              `{receiver, slippage:0.01, inputs, outputs, enableAggregator:true,
 *                aggregators:["kyberswap","okx"], useLimitOrder:false}`
 *              — the EXACT key-set `PendleClient.convertMulti` sends, which is why
 *              no new body key was needed for any of these actions.
 *   Base     : https://api-v2.pendle.finance/core
 *   Date     : 2026-07-28
 *   Cost     : quote-only. Convert BUILDS calldata; it signs nothing, broadcasts
 *              nothing, and needs no key. HTTP 201 on all seven captures.
 *   Chain    : 1, except `transferLiquidityMonad` (chain 143 — the ONE chain whose
 *              reflector differs; see {@link PENDLE_REFLECTOR_PROBES}).
 *   Markets  : chain 1 wstETH 30DEC2027 `0x34280882267ffa6383b363e278b027be083bbe3b`
 *              (PT `0xb253eff1…`, YT `0x04b7fa1e…`, SY `0xcbc72d92…`, underlying
 *              wstETH `0x7f39c581…`) and, for the cross-market actions, wstETH
 *              27AUG2026 `0xba1cbaece600beec76dabc0a4ead31e0339cbe37` (PT
 *              `0xa3e7ccf0…`) — the two share ONE SY, which is what makes the
 *              SY-routed reflect legs appear.
 *              Chain 143 uses sUSDe `0x21422670…` → AUSD `0x6f99cf00…`, which do
 *              NOT share an SY.
 *   Amount   : 1e18 of the input leg on every capture.
 *   Slippage : 100 bps on every capture (see {@link PENDLE_R5D_FIXTURE_SLIPPAGE_BPS}).
 *   Decimals : every chain-1 leg above is 18-decimals (PT/YT/LP/SY/wstETH all 18),
 *              so the captures' raw amounts read directly. The Monad capture's
 *              output (AUSD) is 6-decimals — recorded here because a raw amount
 *              without its decimals is unreadable (rules/90, Money-Path Discipline),
 *              not because the floor arithmetic uses it: the comparison is
 *              raw-to-raw within ONE token.
 *
 * SCRUB APPLIED
 *   `receiver` / `tx.from` is `0x742d35Cc6634C0532925a3b844Bc454e4438f44e` — the
 *   public exchange address this repo already uses as its pseudonymous Pendle
 *   fixture receiver (`fixtures.ts`, `floor-fixtures.ts`). No wallet of ours
 *   appears and no position was read: a convert quote is built for whatever
 *   receiver it is handed. Every other value is public protocol data reproduced
 *   verbatim. NOTHING was removed or edited — a scrubbed field would break the
 *   decode these fixtures exist to exercise.
 *
 * ROUTE LISTS TRUNCATED, VALUES NOT: each capture keeps its first two routes.
 * Every RETAINED route is byte-for-byte what the API returned.
 *
 * NON-EMPTY BY CONSTRUCTION (rule 90, "Verification Discipline"): every capture
 * carries at least one route with real calldata and a real min-out.
 *
 * WHAT THEY PROVE (measured 2026-07-28, not assumed):
 *   - `redeem-sy` — never probed before this card — is SERVED: HTTP 201,
 *     `redeemSyToToken`, one output, min-out exactly on our floor.
 *   - Six of the nine new min-out fields sit EXACTLY on
 *     `floor(output × (10000 − 100) / 10000)` (delta 0). The three LP-add-shaped
 *     ones (`minLpOut`/`minYtOut` on keep-YT, the transfer's final `minLpOut`)
 *     sit ABOVE our floor — they err SAFE, the same way `addLiquiditySingleToken`
 *     does in the R5a captures.
 *   - The provider's `outputs` ORDER is its own canonical order and does NOT
 *     follow the request's: asking `[underlying, PT]` and `[PT, underlying]` both
 *     returned `[PT, underlying]`, and `[market, YT]` / `[YT, market]` both
 *     returned `[market, YT]`. This is why the dual binding rows resolve their
 *     output BY TOKEN and never by index — see `calldata/price-floor.ts`.
 *   - `roll-over-pt` and `transfer-liquidity` are the ONLY callAndReflect actions.
 *     `convert-lp-to-pt` is a PLAIN single-leg `removeLiquiditySinglePt` — the
 *     card's "callAndReflect trio" is in fact a PAIR.
 *   - A reflect action's inner selectors depend on whether the two markets share
 *     an SY: same SY → the SY-routed legs, different SY (the Monad capture) → the
 *     already-pinned `removeLiquiditySingleToken` / `addLiquiditySingleToken`.
 */

